{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/w8ibt7","slideIndex":2,"text":"About 10 minutes, including teacher practice. Switch to your browser at https://www.kaizenmaths.com/#/tools. Keep this slide as your checklist. 1. Teaching Tools: choose a familiar school topic such as fractions, percentages or ratio. Generate a small set and show an answer with its worked solution. 2. Ready-Made Resources: choose a relevant collection and open a Student Pack, then its Teacher Pack. Keep existing print assets ready in case the connection fails. 3. If time allows, open Build a Worksheet, add a question block, show the answers/worked-solution controls and print preview. Then give teachers two minutes to sign in with their arranged access and find a resource for the coming week. Confirm access individually without projecting credentials. Screenshot source: output/resource-navigation-preview.png, a real site screenshot in this repository. It illustrates the workspace navigation and is not a live browser view."}
