{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/sn4i1n","slideIndex":3,"text":"About 2 minutes. Explain that Make It Count supports how teachers teach mathematics, alongside their use of resources. Bar modelling is the initial focus. Ask: If three quarters of a quantity is 18, how could a bar help us find the whole? Invite a teacher to describe the three equal parts, one part and the complete quantity. The answer is 24. Emphasise the reference whole, equal parts and the relationships between quantities. Teachers can study worked examples, attempt challenges and discuss explanations. This is professional learning support, not a promise of a formal qualification. Sources: the bar-modelling pilot course in assets/courses and the programme aims supplied in this conversation. Programme artwork: assets/brand/make-it-count-brighter-futures.png."}
