{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/b42a1f","slideIndex":4,"text":"About 2 minutes. Present this as a proposed structure, not a confirmed calendar. Confirm the school’s priorities, availability and participating teachers. Access/onboarding can begin before professional-development sessions. Initial and final reflections can help us understand changes in confidence and practice, but do not establish that the programme caused any changes. Ask for a short anonymous classroom example or teacher reflection, without pupil names. Agree any research participation, consent and use of findings separately before collecting data for research. Do not present routine course participation as consent to a research study. The six-week intention and reflective approach come from the programme discussion in this conversation."}
